   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The perspective with được and bị",
     "texto": [
      "**Được** and **bị** can present what happens to someone as favourable or unfavourable for that person: **được nghỉ hè** = to have the summer off; **bị ốm** = to fall ill. It's a frequent orientation, not a fixed translation of “good” and “bad”.",
      "In a passive, the person or thing affected goes first: **Em Tuấn được mẹ khen.** = Tuấn's mother praised him (presented as favourable). **Bố tôi bị công an phạt.** = The police fined my father (unfavourable).",
      "The passive is not compulsory in Vietnamese; the active word order is usually enough. After a verb, **được** can also mean “can”: **Tôi nói được tiếng Việt.**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Because… so: vì … nên",
     "texto": [
      "**vì** = because · **nên** = so. They can be used together or separately:",
      "**Vì trời lạnh nên chúng tôi không đi chơi.** = As it was cold, we didn't go out.",
      "**Trời lạnh nên chúng tôi không đi chơi.** = It was cold, so we didn't go out.",
      "**Chúng tôi không đi chơi vì trời lạnh.** = We didn't go out because it was cold."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
